  "result": "I graded quiz 0001 and wrote `grades/0001-s1.json`. You got 1 of 3 right.\n\n- **q1: wrong (M2).** You picked (a), that pipelining makes one instruction faster. It doesn't. One instruction still takes the same time, but more instructions finish in a given time.\n- **q2: wrong.** You said 100, but the answer is 103. The first instruction needs 4 cycles to go through all 4 stages, then the other 99 finish one per cycle: 4 + 99 = 103.\n- **q3: right.** Instructions overlap, so the total time shrinks.\n\nYou've got the core reason pipelining helps: instructions overlap. Next, redo q2 by drawing a 4-stage, 5-instruction timeline and counting the cycles. It should come to 8, which you can check against 4 + (5 − 1).\n\nI wrote the final file by copying the last draft, but I didn't re-parse it as JSON. I did read the draft back as valid JSON before that. The second review pass said \"fix\", and I applied its two fixes without a third review. I also added `learning-records/0002-pipelining-and-single-instruction-time.md`, updated `NOTES.md` and wrote `review-records/0001-s1-grade.md`.",
